      "retrieved_evidence": "[1] biomedicines-11-03080 (data/biomedicines-11-03080.pdf, chunk 4, score 1.113)\nsitting in the S2 binding pocket. Encouraged from the crys- tal structure results, they went on to synthesize the ADCs, anti-Her2-mc-cBuCitPABC-MMAE, and anti-Her2-mc-ValCitPABC-MMAE (Figure 3B), using an engineered cysteine strategy with DAR between 1.8 and 2.0. When these ADCs were evaluated against Her-2-expressing SKBR-3 cells, both ADCs showed almost similar antigen dependent anti-cancer activity and were equally stable in thein vivo mouse models. When incubating the ValCit and cBuCit ADCs with inhibitors of cathepsin B, they found that cBuCit cleavage activity was reduced by 90% vs. 50% for ValCit, demonstrating the high specificity of the cBuCit linker towards cathepsin B. Biomedicines 2023, 11, 3080 6 of 14 Biomedicines 2023, 10, x FOR PEER REVIEW 6 of 15 90% vs. 50% for ValCit, demonstrating the high specificity of the cBuCit linker towards cathepsin B. Figure 2. Various Linker payload designs for..."
